<title>SINGAPORE: Lum Chang SI buys London property.</title>
<headline>Lum Chang SI buys London property.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lum Chang Holdings Ltd said on Monday its 60 percent-owned subsidiary, L.C. (London) Ltd, has bought a London property and its related business for 13.88 million sterling.</p>
<p>Lum Chang said in a statement the purchase of Huntingdon House, which has 50 flats operated as serviced apartments, and its related business was made from Huntingdon House Ltd and London Properties Ltd on May 1.</p>
<p>It said the purchase was funded by a seven-year term loan facility of 14 million sterling from the London branch of Singapore's Overseas Union Bank Ltd.  </p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
